Subject: [PATCH 6/8] test(real catalog): folder counts from the location; the
 catalog's own most common camera
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The real-catalog pass (SPKLIB_C1_CATALOG) failed 3 checks on the Capture One
16.6.4 for Windows test catalog, all in the test's own reading, none in spklib:

- every collection / copy counts: the oracle counted a folder's images from
  ZIMAGEINCOLLECTION. A Mac catalog lists folder members there (and they
  agree with the locations); Capture One for Windows lists none, so the
  oracle said 0 where the folders hold 3 (Day1, Day2 子文件夹). A folder's
  images are now those whose location it is -- what spklib returns and
  Capture One shows -- and an album's are still its ZIMAGEINCOLLECTION rows.
- facets: the check looked up "NIKON Z 8", the owner's camera, and compared
  -1 (absent) with 0. It now takes the catalog's most common camera model,
  so any catalog can be the real one.

docs/CAPTURE-ONE-CATALOG.md records the missing folder rows.

Gate: Linux suite 540 passed, 0 failed. Real-catalog pass on the synthetic
catalog: these checks pass (the two left failing are the synthetic catalog's
missing creation dates, as before).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01EsiBMQLFocprcmVfDPxXCc
